{"course": {"id": "s14", "title": "Camday – Cambridge Primary Mathematics — Stage 4", "units": [{"n": 1, "t": "Numbers and the Number System"}, {"n": 2, "t": "Time and Timetables"}, {"n": 3, "t": "Addition and Subtraction of Whole Numbers"}, {"n": 4, "t": "Probability"}, {"n": 5, "t": "Multiplication, Multiples and Factors"}, {"n": 6, "t": "2D Shapes"}, {"n": 7, "t": "Fractions"}, {"n": 8, "t": "Angles"}, {"n": 9, "t": "Comparing, Rounding and Dividing"}, {"n": 10, "t": "Collecting and Recording Data"}, {"n": 11, "t": "Fractions and Percentages"}, {"n": 12, "t": "Investigating 3D Shapes and Nets"}, {"n": 13, "t": "Addition and Subtraction"}, {"n": 14, "t": "Area and Perimeter"}, {"n": 15, "t": "Special Numbers"}, {"n": 16, "t": "Data Display and Interpretation"}, {"n": 17, "t": "Multiplication and Division"}, {"n": 18, "t": "Position, Direction and Movement"}]}, "unit": {"n": 18, "stage": 14, "title": "Position, Direction and Movement", "strandShort": "Geometry and measure", "blurb": "Coordinates in the first quadrant, compass directions including NE, NW, SE and SW, translations, and reflecting shapes in mirror lines.", "strand": "Geometry and measure", "framework": "Cambridge Primary Mathematics (0096), Stage 4", "lesson": true, "subject": "maths", "read": "media/read/m4u18.pdf"}, "objectives": {"O1": {"code": "4Gp.01", "sec": "18.1", "codeNote": "", "t": "Read and plot coordinates, use compass directions and describe translations."}, "O2": {"code": "4Gp.02", "sec": "18.2", "codeNote": "", "t": "Reflect 2D shapes in horizontal and vertical mirror lines."}}, "sections": [{"id": "18.1", "title": "Position and movement", "objs": ["O1"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Park map", "p": ["On a park map the café is at **(2, 5)** and the playground at **(6, 1)**. North is at the top.", "Which direction do you walk from the café to the playground? Think before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Grids", "p": ["Across first, then up."], "qq": {"id": "m4u18s1t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "In (2, 5), how far across?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 2, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "2."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Coordinates", "p": ["A point on a grid is written **(across, up)**. Start at (0, 0), go **across** the x-axis, then **up** the y-axis."], "fig": {"kind": "coord", "x": [0, 7], "y": [0, 6], "points": [{"x": 2, "y": 5, "l": "café"}, {"x": 6, "y": 1, "l": "play"}]}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Compass directions and translations", "p": ["The four compass directions: **north** (up), **east** (right), **south** (down), **west** (left).", "Moving a point or shape without turning it is a **translation**: café (2, 5) → playground (6, 1) is **4 east and 4 south** (4 right, 4 down)."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Read", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m4u18s1t02", "type": "short", "prompt": "Point 3 across and 4 up?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(3, 4)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*3\\s*[,;]\\s*4\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": "(3, 4)."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I use coordinates and directions?", "p": ["Step 1: Read across (x) first, then up (y).", "Step 2: Right = east, left = west, up = north, down = south.", "Step 3: Count squares to describe a move.", "Step 4: In a translation every point moves the same way."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Plot", "p": [], "q": "Plot (4, 0).", "steps": [["4 across, 0 up", ""]], "a": "on the x-axis"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Direction", "p": [], "q": "From (1, 1) to (1, 5).", "steps": [["x the same, y up 4", ""]], "a": "4 north"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Translate", "p": [], "q": "(3, 2) moves 2 east and 3 north.", "steps": [["x + 2 = 5", ""], ["y + 3 = 5", ""]], "a": "(5, 5)"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Describe", "p": [], "q": "(6, 4) → (2, 4).", "steps": [["x down by 4", ""]], "a": "4 west"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Translate", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m4u18s1t03", "type": "short", "prompt": "(1, 3) moves 3 east?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(4, 3)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*4\\s*[,;]\\s*3\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": "(4, 3)."}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Up before across", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "Point 2 across and 5 up.", "lines": ["(5, 2)"], "bad": 0, "why": "Across comes first: (2, 5).", "fix": [["(2, 5)", ""]], "id": "m4u18s1t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Writing (up, across)", "p": ["Along the corridor, then up the stairs."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Maps, treasure hunts, board games and robots use coordinates and compass directions."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["(across, up).", "N up, E right, S down, W left.", "Translation: slide, no turning."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 660, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "18.1-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m4u18s1k01", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Before you read on: café to playground goes…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "east and south", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "west and north", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"id": "18.1-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m4u18s1k02", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Right on a map (north at the top) is…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "north", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "east", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "south", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "west", "ok": false, "fb": ""}], "fixed": true}}, {"id": "18.1-k3", "t": 3, "after": 9, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m4u18s1k03", "type": "short", "prompt": "(3, 2) moves 2 east and 3 north?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(5, 5)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*5\\s*[,;]\\s*5\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "18.1-k4", "t": 4, "after": 14, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m4u18s1k04", "type": "short", "prompt": "Quick check: 2 across, 5 up?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(2, 5)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*2\\s*[,;]\\s*5\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}}], "captions": [], "chapters": [[0, 300]], "req": [{"id": "m4u18s1r01", "type": "short", "prompt": "4 across, 1 up?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(4, 1)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*4\\s*[,;]\\s*1\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u18s1r02", "type": "short", "prompt": "0 across, 3 up?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(0, 3)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*0\\s*[,;]\\s*3\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u18s1r03", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Down the map is…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "north", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "east", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "south", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "west", "ok": false, "fb": ""}], "fixed": true}, {"id": "m4u18s1r04", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Left on the map is…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "north", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "east", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "south", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "west", "ok": true, "fb": ""}], "fixed": true}, {"id": "m4u18s1r05", "type": "short", "prompt": "(2, 2) moves 3 north?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(2, 5)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*2\\s*[,;]\\s*5\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u18s1r06", "type": "short", "prompt": "(5, 4) moves 2 west?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(3, 4)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*3\\s*[,;]\\s*4\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u18s1r07", "type": "short", "prompt": "(6, 6) moves 4 south?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(6, 2)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*6\\s*[,;]\\s*2\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u18s1r08", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "(1, 1) → (5, 1) is a move…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "north", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "east", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "south", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "west", "ok": false, "fb": ""}], "fixed": true}], "prac": [{"id": "m4u18s1p01", "type": "short", "prompt": "(3, 1) moves 2 east and 4 north?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(5, 5)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*5\\s*[,;]\\s*5\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u18s1p02", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "(5, 6) → (2, 3) is…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "3 west, 3 south", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "3 east, 3 north", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m4u18s1p03", "type": "short", "prompt": "A square has corners (1, 1), (3, 1), (3, 3). Fourth?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(1, 3)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*1\\s*[,;]\\s*3\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u18s1p04", "type": "explain", "prompt": "Explain how to get from (2, 5) to (6, 1).", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "rubric": [{"pt": "4 east/right", "kw": ["4 ?(east|right)"]}, {"pt": "4 south/down", "kw": ["4 ?(south|down)"]}], "need": 2, "model": "Move 4 east (right) and 4 south (down).", "hint": "", "reason": "Move 4 east (right) and 4 south (down)."}, {"id": "m4u18s1p05", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Facing north, turn a half turn. Now facing…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "north", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "east", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "south", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "west", "ok": false, "fb": ""}], "fixed": true}, {"id": "m4u18s1p06", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Facing east, turn a quarter turn clockwise. Now facing…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "north", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "east", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "south", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "west", "ok": false, "fb": ""}], "fixed": true}, {"id": "m4u18s1p07", "type": "short", "prompt": "Triangle (1, 1), (3, 1), (1, 4) moves 2 east. New position of (1, 4)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(3, 4)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*3\\s*[,;]\\s*4\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u18s1p08", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "In a translation the shape…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "does not turn", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "turns", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}], "adv": [{"id": "m4u18s1a01", "type": "short", "prompt": "* Advanced. A robot at (0, 0) goes 3 N, 5 E, 1 S, 2 W. Where is it?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(3, 2)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*3\\s*[,;]\\s*2\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u18s1a02", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "* Advanced. Facing west, turn three quarter turns clockwise. Now facing…", "diff": "VH", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "north", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "east", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "south", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "west", "ok": false, "fb": ""}], "fixed": true}, {"id": "m4u18s1a03", "type": "explain", "prompt": "* Advanced. Give directions for a robot from (1, 1) to (4, 6) using only N and E.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "rubric": [{"pt": "3 E", "kw": ["3 ?e"]}, {"pt": "5 N", "kw": ["5 ?n"]}], "need": 2, "model": "3 east and 5 north (in any order).", "hint": "", "reason": "3 east and 5 north (in any order)."}], "more": [{"id": "m4u18s1m01", "type": "short", "prompt": "1 across, 2 up?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(1, 2)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*1\\s*[,;]\\s*2\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u18s1m02", "type": "short", "prompt": "5 across, 5 up?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(5, 5)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*5\\s*[,;]\\s*5\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u18s1m03", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Up the map is…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "north", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "east", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "south", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "west", "ok": false, "fb": ""}], "fixed": true}, {"id": "m4u18s1m04", "type": "short", "prompt": "(1, 1) moves 1 east?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(2, 1)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*2\\s*[,;]\\s*1\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u18s1m05", "type": "short", "prompt": "(3, 3) moves 1 south?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(3, 2)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*3\\s*[,;]\\s*2\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u18s1m06", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "First number in a coordinate is…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "across", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "up", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}], "notes": "v4", "pdf": [{"book": "c4u18", "p0": 2, "p1": 5, "label": "pages 2–5", "title": "Lesson 18.1 notes · Position and movement", "note": "The whole lesson as a document you can print, then Practice on paper with answers at the back.", "look": []}]}, {"id": "18.2", "title": "Reflecting 2D shapes", "objs": ["O2"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Mirror writing", "p": ["Hold a picture of a shape against a mirror. The reflection looks flipped.", "How far behind the mirror does each corner seem to be? Think before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Symmetry", "p": ["A line of symmetry splits a shape into matching halves."], "qq": {"id": "m4u18s2t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Lines of symmetry in a square?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 4, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "4."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Reflection", "p": ["A **reflection** flips a shape over a **mirror line**. Each point of the image is the **same distance** from the mirror line as the original, on the **other side**."], "fig": {"kind": "cells", "cells": [[0, 0], [1, 0], [0, 1], [0, 2], [5, 0], [4, 0], [5, 1], [5, 2]], "cols": 6, "rows": 3, "grid": true, "mirror": {"x": 3}}, "p2": ["The L-shape on the left is reflected in the vertical line to make the shape on the right."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Horizontal mirror lines", "p": ["With a **horizontal** mirror line, squares above move the same distance **below** the line (and vice versa).", "The reflected shape is the same size but faces the opposite way."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Distance", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m4u18s2t02", "type": "num", "prompt": "A corner is 3 squares left of a vertical mirror line. How far right is its image?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "3."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I reflect a shape?", "p": ["Step 1: Reflect one corner at a time.", "Step 2: Count squares from the corner to the mirror line.", "Step 3: Count the same number on the other side.", "Step 4: Join the new corners; check the shape is flipped."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Vertical line", "p": [], "q": "A square 1 square left of the line.", "steps": [["same distance on the right", ""]], "a": "1 square right of the line"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Touching the line", "p": [], "q": "A corner on the mirror line.", "steps": [["distance 0", ""]], "a": "stays on the line"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Horizontal line", "p": [], "q": "A point 2 squares above the line.", "steps": [["2 squares below", ""]], "a": "2 below"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Check", "p": [], "q": "Does the image face the same way?", "steps": [["flipped", ""]], "a": "no – it faces the opposite way"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Horizontal", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m4u18s2t03", "type": "num", "prompt": "A point 4 squares below a horizontal mirror line. How far above is its image?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 4, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "4."}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Sliding instead of flipping", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "Reflect an arrow pointing right in a vertical mirror line.", "lines": ["The image points right too."], "bad": 0, "why": "A reflection flips it: the image points left.", "fix": [["points left", ""]], "id": "m4u18s2t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Sliding the shape instead of flipping it", "p": ["Measure each point's distance to the line."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Lakes reflect mountains; the word AMBULANCE is printed backwards so drivers read it in their mirror."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["Same distance from the mirror line, other side.", "Reflect corner by corner.", "The image is flipped."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 660, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "18.2-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m4u18s2k01", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Before you read on: the reflection is…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "the same distance behind", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "twice as far", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"id": "18.2-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m4u18s2k02", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Is the reflected shape the same size?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "yes", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "no", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"id": "18.2-k3", "t": 3, "after": 9, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m4u18s2k03", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "A corner on the mirror line…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "stays on the line", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, 